        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, thank you for entrusting us with the care of your 73-year-old female patient, admitted on 03/04/2019 with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included arterial blood gas analysis confirming hypoxaemic respiratory failure, chest X-ray excluding pneumonia or pneumothorax, and pulse oximetry monitoring throughout her stay. Blood tests revealed mild systemic inflammation. Treatment consisted of supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluid support. She responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. Prior to discharge, patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided. We recommend continuation of her inhaled maintenance therapy and close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact us should you have any questions.</div>"
            },
